I did; it's cumulative by weight of creature killed until you reach 100%,
at which point it's "full".

(Having resistance wear off as you take damage is intriguing but is
risky; players aren't going to want to carry corpses around just to
reload their resistances constantly.)

> Perhaps fire resistance or immunity causes vulnerability to cold, or
> prevents cold resistance or immunity.  For instance, maybe getting fire
> resistance cancels a like amount of cold resistance (and vice-versa);
> fire immunity might mean you take extra damage from cold.

POWDER uses this; things which grant you fire resistance may also grant
you vulnerability to cold.  But, POWDER's resistances and
vulnerabilities both wear off after a certain number of turns, and if
the vulnerability wears off while the resistance doesn't, it really
wasn't much of a weakness at all.

